{% comment %}
  A numbered agenda ledger. The mockup's .agledger.

  It replaced the day cards. Two cards, each holding its own bulleted list, made
  the schedule read as two parallel options; a single ledger reads as one run of
  events in order, which is what a two-day seminar actually is.

  THE NUMBERING IS CONTINUOUS across the whole ledger -- 01 to 11, not 01 to 05
  then 01 to 06 -- so it counts sessions rather than restarting per day. That is
  why the numbers are rendered from a running counter here rather than from an
  <ol>: the day headers sit between items and would either take a number of
  their own or break the sequence.

  Blocks are flat in Shopify, so a day cannot contain its items. Order is the
  only thing binding an item to the day above it. Reordering a Day block in the
  editor moves the divider, not the items -- move the items too.

  ELEMENT. The root is a <div>: `"tag": "section"` already wraps this. The
  ledger inside is a <dl>: each day is a term and its sessions are its
  descriptions, which is the closest native pairing for "heading with a list of
  things under it" that survives being flattened into one element.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign classes = 'suf-section'
  if section.settings.anchor != blank
    assign classes = classes | append: ' suf-anchor-target'
  endif
-%}

<div class="{{ classes }}" {% if section.settings.anchor != blank %}id="{{ section.settings.anchor | handle }}"{% endif %}>
  <div class="suf-wrap">
    <dl class="suf-agenda">
      {%- assign n = 0 -%}
      {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
        {%- case block.type -%}
          {%- when 'day' -%}
            <dt class="suf-agenda__day" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
              {%- if block.settings.badge != blank -%}
                <span class="suf-agenda__badge">{{ block.settings.badge | escape }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if block.settings.heading != blank -%}
                <span class="suf-agenda__dayname">
                  {%- render 'suf-nb', text: block.settings.heading -%}
                </span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </dt>

          {%- when 'item' -%}
            {%- assign n = n | plus: 1 -%}
            <dd class="suf-agenda__row" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
              {%- comment -%}
                Decorative: the sequence is already carried by the list order,
                and "zero one" read before every line is noise.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <span class="suf-agenda__n" aria-hidden="true">
                {{- n | prepend: '0' | slice: -2, 2 -}}
              </span>
              <span class="suf-agenda__text">
                {%- assign text = block.settings.text | escape -%}
                {%- render 'suf-nb', text: text -%}
              </span>
            </dd>
        {%- endcase -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </dl>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Agenda ledger (SUF)",
  "tag": "section",
  "max_blocks": 30,
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "anchor", "label": "Anchor id" }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "day",
      "name": "Day divider",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "badge", "label": "Badge", "info": "e.g. \"Day 1\"." },
        { "type": "inline_richtext", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "item",
      "name": "Session",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "text",
          "label": "Session",
          "info": "Numbered automatically, counting on from the session above -- the count does not restart on a new day."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Agenda ledger (SUF)",
      "blocks": [{ "type": "day" }, { "type": "item" }, { "type": "item" }]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
